  "summary": "Suffolk County lawmakers questioned Flock Safety representatives at a Public Safety Committee hearing about privacy, data access, and potential misuse of the company's ALPR technology, which is used by Suffolk County PD, the sheriff's office, and East End agencies. Flock defended the tool as legally vetted and said agencies control the data and all searches are audited. Separately, the county recently paused a proposed $4 million Flock gunshot-detection agreement.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Isn't it true you've constructed a nationwide surveillance network capable of reconstructing an individual's movements over time?",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "The courts have found it's not a surveillance tool that can track a person's course of daily life.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "If someone here were to do like has been reported in other places in the country and run their boyfriend or girlfriend a thousand times, they're going to go to jail",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
